### Set status code and headers on @Sse() route

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/http/server-sent-events.md

Set a custom status code and headers on an SSE route by injecting the response with @Res({ passthrough: true }). Starting with NestJS v12.1.3, the status code and headers set before the stream starts are sent. On Fastify, use the FastifyReply type instead of Response.

```typescript
@Sse('sse')
sse(@Res({ passthrough: true }) res: Response): Observable<MessageEvent> {
  res.status(202);
  res.header('x-version', '1.0.0');
  return interval(1000).pipe(map((_) => ({ data: { hello: 'world' } })));
}
```
